# The local working copy of the environment files. README.md tells a contributor
# to copy packages/database/.env.example to .env before running anything, and
# `pnpm verify` then fails on the very file it just told them to write, because
# check:secrets passes --no-gitignore and so scans it. Ignoring these loses no
# real protection: .gitignore already keeps both out of a commit, and Gitleaks
# and GitGuardian run over the pushed history in CI, so a secret that ever
# reached the repository is still caught. This only stops the scanner reading a
# developer's own untracked file.
.env
packages/database/.env
